{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","title":"unixNew(unix:)","roleHeading":"Type Method","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib9IOChannelC7unixNew0C0ACSgSi_tFZ","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"unixNew","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"unix","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"IOChannel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib9IOChannelC"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/iochannel\/unixnew(unix:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel\/unixNew(unix:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel"},{"type":"text","text":" given a file descriptor. On UNIX systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this works for plain files, pipes, and sockets."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"unixNew","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"unix"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"fd","kind":"internalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel","text":"IOChannel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib9IOChannelC"},{"text":"!","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The returned "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" has a reference count of 1."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default encoding for ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel"},{"type":"text","text":" is UTF-8. If your application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is reading output from a command using via pipe, you may need to set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the encoding to the encoding of the current locale (see","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_get_charset()"},{"type":"text","text":") with the "},{"code":"g_io_channel_set_encoding()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the fd passed will not be closed when the final reference","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel"},{"type":"text","text":" data structure is dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you want to read raw binary data without interpretation, then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"call the "},{"code":"g_io_channel_set_encoding()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoding argument."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function is available in GLib on Windows, too, but you should"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"avoid using it on Windows. The domain of file descriptors and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sockets overlap. There is no way for GLib to know which one you mean","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"in case the argument you pass to this function happens to be both a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"valid file descriptor and socket. If that happens a warning is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"issued, and GLib assumes that it is the file descriptor you mean."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/IOChannel":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/iochannel","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/IOChannel","title":"IOChannel","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IOChannel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"IOChannel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"GIOChannel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" data type aims to provide a portable method for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"using file descriptors, pipes, and sockets, and integrating them"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"into the main event loop (see [struct"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"]). Currently,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full support is available on UNIX platforms; support for Windows","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is only partially complete.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/IOChannel/unixNew(unix:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","t